---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="How It Works" description="How DOCHECK checks your file against published form requirements and fixes common issues in your browser.">
  <p><a href="/">← Back to checker</a></p>
  <div class="prose">
    <h1>How It Works</h1>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>Choose your category and form.</strong> Exams, identity documents, or bank &amp; KYC — then the exact form, like SSC CGL or PAN Card.</li>
      <li><strong>Upload your file.</strong> It is read inside your browser: size, dimensions and format. Nothing is sent to a server.</li>
      <li><strong>Read the verdict.</strong> PASS, or a row-by-row report showing your file against each published requirement.</li>
      <li><strong>Fix in one click.</strong> Resize, compress or convert your file to meet the selected requirements, compare before and after, then download.</li>
    </ol>
    <h2>Where the numbers come from</h2>
    <p>Every requirement value is tied to a named official source with a verification date. Where official sources disagree, we show the conflict instead of silently picking one number.</p>
    <h2>What we never claim</h2>
    <p>We never promise a portal will accept your file. Our language is always: “Meets the published requirements we verified as of [date].” The live application portal is the final authority.</p>
    <p><a class="btn-primary" href="/#check" style="display:inline-block;width:auto;text-decoration:none;padding:12px 26px;">Check a File</a></p>
  </div>
</Base>
